ginal code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\\n1: #!/bin/bash\\n2: # check.sh — the ONLY command an agent may run.\\n3: #\\n4: #   /abs/path/tools/antigravity/check.sh FILE.lean\\n5: #\\n6: # Lives outside every agent workspace and is hashed by guard.sh: agents can\\n7: # write inside their workspace, so a checker kept there could be rewritten into\\n8: # anything. It screens the file first (tools/antigravity_handoff.py lint), because\\n9: # Lean elaboration can itself run shell commands; then elaborates it with bare\\n10: # `lean` and an explicit LEAN_PATH, and prints every theorem's axioms. Nothing\\n11: # here depends on $HOME — agents run under a private one — and `lake` is never\\n12: # involved (in this project lake deletes Mathlib when it cannot re-clone).\\n13: set -uo pipefail\\n14: f=\\\"${1:?usage: check.sh FILE.lean}\\\"\\n15: [ -f \\\"$f\\\" ] || { echo \\\"CHECK: no such file: $f\\\"; exit 2; }\\n16: \\n17: ROOT=\\\"$(cd \\\"$(dirname \\\"$(readlink -f \\\"$0\\\")\\\")/../..\\\" && pwd)\\\"\\n18: # Tool paths come from a protected file, not from the home directory: agents run\\n19: # under a private HOME, and on compute nodes `getent passwd` reports a different\\n20: # home (/home/<user>@ad…) than the one the tools live in.\\n21: ENVF=\\\"$ROOT/handoff/.agf_env\\\"\\n22: export ELAN_HOME=\\\"$(grep -m1 '^AGF_ELAN_HOME=' \\\"$ENVF\\\" 2>/dev/null | cut -d= -f2-)\\\"\\n23: LEAN=\\\"$ELAN_HOME/bin/lean\\\"\\n24: [ -x \\\"$LEAN\\\" ] || { echo \\\"CHECK: lean not found (ELAN_HOME='$ELAN_HOME' from $ENVF)\\\"; exit 2; }\\n25: PY=\\\"$ROOT/.venv/bin/python\\\"\\n26: LP_FILE=\\\"$ROOT/handoff/.agf_lean_path\\\"\\n27: [ -s \\\"$LP_FILE\\\" ] || { echo \\\"CHECK: missing $LP_FILE\\\"; exit 2; }\\n28: export LEAN_PATH=\\\"$(cat \\\"$LP_FILE\\\")\\\"\\n29: \\n30: orig=\\\"$(ls \\\"$ROOT\\\"/benchmark/challenges_*/\\\"$(basename \\\"$f\\\")\\\" 2>/dev/null | head -1)\\\"\\n31: if ! \\\"$PY\\\" \\\"$ROOT/tools/antigravity_handoff.py\\\" lint ${orig:+--original \\\"$orig\\\"} \\\"$f\\\"; then\\n32:   echo \\\"CHECK: refused to elaborate — remove the construct named above.\\\"\\n33:   exit 3\\n34: fi\\n35: \\n36: tmp=\\\"$(mktemp --suffix=.lean)\\\"\\n37: cp \\\"$f\\\" \\\"$tmp\\\"\\n38: for t in $(grep -oE '^theorem +[A-Za-z0-9_]+' \\\"$f\\\" | awk '{print $2}'); do\\n39:   echo \\\"#print axioms $t\\\" >> \\\"$tmp\\\"\\n40: done\\n41: timeout 1800 \\\"$LEAN\\\" \\\"$tmp\\\"\\n42: rc=$?\\n43: rm -f \\\"$tmp\\\"\\n44: if [ $rc -eq 0 ]; then\\n45:   echo \\\"CHECK: elaborated. Allowed axioms: propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound.\\\"\\n46:   echo \\\"       'sorryAx' in a list above means that theorem is unfinished.\\\"\\n47: else\\n48:   echo \\\"CHECK: FAILED (exit $rc)\\\"\\n49: fi\\n50: exit $rc\\n51: \\nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\\n\"}\n16: {\"step_index\":15,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T14:53:29Z\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/reference/GraphInvariantsComputable.lean\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"250\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing file\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View GraphInvariantsComputable.lean lines 1-250\\\"\"}}]}\n17: {\"step_index\":16,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"GENERIC\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T14:53:31Z\",\"content\":\"Created At: 2026-09-11T16:53:31+02:00\\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T16:53:31+02:00\\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/reference/GraphInvariantsComputable.lean`\\nTotal Lines: 537\\nTotal Bytes: 27292\\nShowing lines 1 to 250\\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\\n1: /-\\n2: GraphInvariantsComputable.lean — a *computable* mirror of the invariants in\\n3: `GraphInvariants.lean`, so that a claim about one explicit finite graph can be\\n4: settled by `decide` rather than by a hand proof.\\n5: \\n6: Why this file exists\\n7: --------------------\\n8: `GraphInvariants.lean` defines the invariants the way a mathematician states\\n9: them: `dominationNumber G = sInf { n | ∃ s, s.card = n ∧ G.IsDominatingSet s }`.\\n10: That is the right *specification*, but `sInf` over a `Set ℕ` (under\\n11: `open scoped Classical`) is **noncomputable**, so the kernel cannot evaluate it\\n12: on a concrete graph — measured directly, `decide` succeeds on `order`, `size`\\n13: and `minDegree`, and fails on every `sInf`/`sSup` invariant (domination,\\n14: annihilation, the zero-forcing family, and mathlib's own `indepNum`/`cliqueNum`).\\n15: \\n16: That blocks the cheapest source of formal results we have. The refutation engine\\n17: kills thousands of candidates and knows exactly which graph kills each one; each\\n18: such pair is a `¬∀ …` theorem whose proof is \\\"evaluate both sides on this graph\\\"\\n19: — but only if the invariants actually evaluate.\\n20: \\n21: The definitions here are the same mathematical objects expressed as a minimum\\n22: over an explicitly enumerated `Finset`, which the kernel *can* reduce. They are\\n23: deliberately kept in their own namespace: nothing in the existing proof pipeline\\n24: changes, and `GraphInvariants.lean` remains the specification of record.\\n25: -/\\n26: import Mathlib\\n27: \\n<truncated 10400 bytes>\\n  HasWitness (IsTotalZeroForcingSet G)\\n217: \\n218: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\\n219:     Decidable (HasTotalZeroForcingNumber G) := by\\n220:   unfold HasTotalZeroForcingNumber; infer_instance\\n221: \\n222: /-- One step of reachability inside `S`: everything already in `T`, plus the\\n223: vertices of `S` adjacent to it. -/\\n224: def reachWithin (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S T : Finset V) : Finset V :=\\n225:   T ∪ S.filter (fun w => ∃ v ∈ T, G.Adj v w)\\n226: \\n227: /-- The vertices of `S` reachable from `v` without leaving `S`. Iterating `n`\\n228: times suffices: each step that changes anything adds at least one vertex. -/\\n229: def componentWithin (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S : Finset V) (v : V) :\\n230:     Finset V :=\\n231:   (reachWithin G S)^[Fintype.card V] {v}\\n232: \\n233: /-- `S` induces a connected subgraph.\\n234: \\n235: The specification layer says `(G.induce ↑S).Connected`, which is a statement\\n236: about walks in a subtype and carries no `Decidable` instance. This is the\\n237: decidable equivalent: `S` is nonempty and every vertex of it reaches all of `S`\\n238: from inside. `Connected` is `Preconnected ∧ Nonempty`, so both conjuncts are\\n239: accounted for — the nonemptiness is not incidental. -/\\n240: def IsConnectedSubset (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S : Finset V) : Prop :=\\n241:   S.Nonempty ∧ ∀ v ∈ S, componentWithin G S v = S\\n242: \\n243: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S : Finset V) :\\n244:     Decidable (IsConnectedSubset G S) := by\\n245:   unfold IsConnectedSubset; infer_instance\\n246: \\n247: /-- A connected zero-forcing set: zero-forcing and inducing a connected\\n248: subgraph, matching graphcalc's `is_connected_zero_forcing_set`. -/\\n249: def IsConnectedZeroForcingSet (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S : Finset V) :\\n250:     Prop :=\\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\\n\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}\n18: {\"step_index\":17,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T14:53:31Z\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/mnt/home/japake